**Code Explanation:**

The code loads the analysis results generated in Step 3 and Step 4, as well as the tracer trajectories and the final snapshot VTK file. It then generates three multi-panel figures to consolidate the results: 1. Figure 1 (MSD-related results): Plots the ensemble Mean-Square Displacement (MSD), conditional MSD for 'Trapped' and 'Free' cohorts, the time-dependent power-law exponent alpha(t), and the MSD for 'Boundary-Crossers' vs 'Non-Crossers'. Log-log scales are used for MSD plots to highlight power-law scaling regimes. 2. Figure 2 (Anisotropy and VACF): Plots the anisotropy ratio lambda(t) = MSD_parallel / MSD_perp, the Velocity Autocorrelation Function (VACF), and the Taylor diffusion coefficient over time. 3. Figure 3 (Vortex/FTLE diagnostics): Plots the Q-criterion autocorrelation to show the decorrelation time of trapping events, the distribution of Finite-Time Lyapunov Exponents (FTLE) at the final time, a bar chart comparing the mean FTLE of 'Trapped' vs 'Free' cohorts, and a 3D spatial visualization of a subset of tracer trajectories overlaid with high Q-criterion regions (top 1%) for the final snapshot. All plots are saved at high resolution (300 dpi) in the data/ directory with descriptive filenames and timestamps. The script also prints a summary of the plotted data to the console.

**Modifications:**

Fixed the ValueError by plotting vacf and taylor_diff against t[1:] instead of t. The vacf array has length 199 because it was computed from velocities obtained via finite differences of the trajectories (which reduces the length by 1). Added the missing 3D spatial visualization of tracer trajectories overlaid with high Q-criterion regions for the final snapshot in Figure 3. Ensured all paths use the data/ directory. Wrapped all execution code in the if __name__ == '__main__': block.

